usage: hisar [--standalone] <command> [arguments]

commands:
  status                                                 show whether hisar uses the Hisar app or its own sign-in, and the account
  signup             <invite-link>                       create your account from an invite
  login                                                  sign in on this device
  logout                                                 sign out on this device
  whoami                                                 show the signed-in account
  vaults                                                 list vaults
  vault-create       <name>                              create a shared vault
  vault              rename|delete|leave|create|give|take <vault> rename, delete or leave a vault, create one, or give an organization vault to a team (rename <vault> [name] | delete <vault> [--move-to v | --delete-items --confirm <name>] [-y] | leave <vault> [-y] | create <name> [--org <org> --team <team>] | give <vault> --org <org> --team <team> [-r owner|editor|reader] | take <vault> --org <org> --team <team>)
  ls                 [-v vault] [--tag tag] [--favorites] list items; --tag keeps those with a tag, --favorites lists your favorites in every vault
  get                <item> [-f field] [-v vault]        show an item, or one field of it (e.g. -f password, -f code)
  read               <hisar://vault/item/field> [--no-newline] print one secret, for scripts
  run                [--env-file f]... [--no-masking] -- <cmd> run a command with the secrets its hisar:// references name, masked in its output
  mcp                                                    serve coding agents over MCP (stdio): they use secrets without seeing them, after you approve in the Hisar app
  add                [-v vault] [--type t]               add an item; --type is one of login, secure-note, credit-card, identity, api-credential, address, software-license, server, database (default login)
  edit               <item> [-v vault]                   edit an item
  rm                 <item> [-v vault]                   delete an item
  favorite           <item> [-v vault]                   add an item to your Favorites, on all your devices (only you see them)
  unfavorite         <item> [-v vault]                   remove an item from your Favorites
  import             <file> [-v vault] [-format f] [-y]  import a Hisar export, a 1Password, Bitwarden, LastPass or browser CSV export, or a .env file (--item, --keys, --dry-run)
  export             [-o file] [--format encrypted|plain] export every vault you can open, encrypted with a passphrase you choose or as plain JSON
  generate           [-n length] [-no-symbols]           generate a password
  people                                                 list the people you share vaults with, with their security codes
  share              <vault> <email> [-r role]           invite someone to a vault by email (role: owner, editor, reader)
  unshare            <vault> <email>                     remove someone from a vault and rotate its key
  invitations        [accept|decline|cancel <id>]        list share invitations, answer them, and finish accepted shares
  invite             <email>                             email someone an invite to create a Hisar account
  orgs                                                   list your organizations and invitations to them; gives team members the vault keys they wait for and rotates the vaults someone lost
  org                <action> <org> [arguments]          manage an organization (create <name> | show <org> | rename <org> <name> | delete <org> [-y] | invite <org> <email> [-r admin|member] | cancel <org> <email> | accept [id] | decline [id] | role <org> <email> admin|member | remove <org> <email> [-y] | leave <org> [-y])
  team               <action> <org> <team> [arguments]   manage an organization's teams (create <org> <team> | rename <org> <team> <name> | delete <org> <team> [-y] | add <org> <team> <email> | remove <org> <team> <email>)
  share-link         <item>|--text|open <url>|revoke <id> share an item or text with anyone through an end-to-end encrypted link (--field, --expires 1h|1d|7d|30d, --views, --passphrase)
  share-links                                            list your live share links
  account            change-password|replace-secret-key [-o file]|delete change your master password, replace your Secret Key (with a new Emergency Kit) or delete your account
  emergency-kit      [-o file]                           save your Emergency Kit PDF (sign-in address, email, Secret Key)
  devices                                                list your signed-in devices
  revoke-device      <id>                                sign out a device

hisar uses the Hisar app when it lets the command-line tool use it, and starts the app when it is
installed but not running (HISAR_NO_LAUNCH=1 never starts it); otherwise it signs in on its own. --standalone or HISAR_STANDALONE=1 always signs in on its own.
hisar --version prints the version.
